{# roles/seat seat.yml — drop-in 2 of 2 (HD-445): the PATH a USER unit never gets.
   pi-web shells out to `pi` for the model list, every chat turn and its own
   self-update; no flag overrides the binary path. A systemd USER unit gets no login
   shell, so ~/.profile is never read and the unit's PATH is the sbin/bin defaults.
   TWO directories, because pi has TWO layouts (measured on oldsrv 2026-10-09):
     * seat_pi_bin      — pi's OWN launcher dir (~/.pi/agent/bin over install/releases/);
                          pi 1.1.0's `pi update` migrates an npm -g seat to it.
     * seat_pi_node_bin — the pinned Node tarball's bin dir: the npm -g layout's `pi`
                          symlink lives there, and pi's shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env node`,
                          so a lone `pi` symlink (or ~/.local/bin) fails `env: node: not found`.
   With only ONE of the two the other layout dies with `exec: "pi": executable file not found in
   $PATH` — measured 2026-10-01 (neither dir) and 2026-10-09 (node dir only, right after a
   `pi update` migrated the seat). `current` is a stable symlink, so a Node bump re-points one
   link and this file stays correct. #}
[Service]
Environment=PATH={{ seat_pi_bin }}:{{ seat_pi_node_bin }}:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
